  "statement": "The task is to count the substrings of a string over {a, b, c}, with length up to 10^5, that do not contain \"abc\" as a subsequence. The valid left ends for each right end form a suffix, so a sliding window (two pointers) or a linear DP that tracks the latest start of an \"a\", \"ab\" and \"abc\" subsequence gives each right end's count in O(1).",
